# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 132's class, lane recovery-b4, beside
# `fixedbugs-132-a-comma-after-every-member-is-one-message`. A statement or
# an arm whose line ends with `,` over a line at its own margin was joined
# to it, `continuation_outside_brackets` for a line that goes on with
# nothing. The line ends at its `,` now, and the `,` is the line's one
# message, what stands past its statement.

function f(n: i64) -> i64
    return match n
        0 => 1,  #~ expected_end_of_line
        _ => 2

function main()
    x = 1
    print(x),  #~ expected_end_of_line
    print(f(x))
